1
00:00:10,135 --> 00:00:12,428
SAM: So this is Ruby, huh?
DEAN: She's a demon, Sam.

2
00:00:12,596 --> 00:00:15,598
RUBY: Her name is Lilith.
She doesn't like you very much.

3
00:00:15,766 --> 00:00:17,642
-How long did they give you?
-One year.

4
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:23,064
[GUNSHOT]

5
00:00:55,222 --> 00:00:56,806
Did you know about Dean's deal?

6
00:00:56,974 --> 00:00:59,183
-That Lilith holds the contract?
-Yes.

7
00:00:59,351 --> 00:01:01,644
You got two months.
You're not gonna go to hell.

8
00:01:01,812 --> 00:01:03,604
It's not Ruby. lt's Lilith.

9
00:01:06,692 --> 00:01:09,819
-Where's Ruby?
-l sent her far, far away.

10
00:01:10,696 --> 00:01:11,988
Sic him, boy.

11
00:01:12,823 --> 00:01:14,282
[BARKING]

12
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:15,658
DEAN:
No!

13
00:01:15,826 --> 00:01:26,043
[SCREAMS]

14
00:01:32,009 --> 00:01:34,552
Somebody help me.

15
00:01:38,098 --> 00:01:39,265
Sam!

16
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:45,605
[GASPlNG]

17
00:01:47,399 --> 00:01:49,275
[VOICES HOWLING]

18
00:01:58,410 --> 00:02:00,620
[COUGHlNG]

19
00:02:00,788 --> 00:02:02,872
[LIGHTER CLlCKING]

20
00:02:03,165 --> 00:02:05,249
[PANTlNG]

21
00:02:13,342 --> 00:02:14,759
[IN RASPY VOICE]
Help.

22
00:02:14,927 --> 00:02:16,219
[COUGHS, GASPS]

23
00:02:16,386 --> 00:02:19,597
Help.

24
00:02:26,271 --> 00:02:28,898
[CREAKING]

25
00:02:29,066 --> 00:02:30,900
[GRUNTlNG]

26
00:02:49,086 --> 00:02:52,129
[GASPS, PANTS]

27
00:02:53,632 --> 00:02:55,716
[GRUNTlNG]

28
00:03:01,181 --> 00:03:07,103
Aah!

29
00:03:07,271 --> 00:03:09,355
[PANTlNG]

30
00:04:11,293 --> 00:04:12,501
[KNOCKlNG]

31
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:14,211
Hello?

32
00:04:29,895 --> 00:04:31,896
[BOTTLE CAP CLATTERS]

33
00:04:35,484 --> 00:04:36,734
[EXHALES]

34
00:04:36,902 --> 00:04:38,986
[PANTlNG]

35
00:04:56,838 --> 00:04:58,422
September.

36
00:05:16,942 --> 00:05:18,025
[SCREAMS]

37
00:05:26,493 --> 00:05:27,660
[GASPS]

38
00:06:20,881 --> 00:06:22,965
[STATIC HISSlNG]

39
00:06:29,598 --> 00:06:32,224
[COWBOY TUNE PLAYS OVER RADIO]

40
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:53,579
[HlGH-PITCHED HUM]

41
00:06:53,747 --> 00:06:59,043
[GRUNTS]

42
00:06:59,211 --> 00:07:00,461
[GLASS SHATTERlNG]

43
00:07:20,816 --> 00:07:22,900
[WlND HOWLlNG]

44
00:07:29,533 --> 00:07:30,574
[PHONE BEEPS]

45
00:07:30,742 --> 00:07:32,201
WOMAN [ON RECORDlNG]:
We're sorry...

46
00:07:32,369 --> 00:07:34,995
...you have reached a number
that has been disconnected.

47
00:07:40,544 --> 00:07:42,002
[LINE RINGlNG]

48
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:43,295
BOBBY:
Yeah?

49
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:44,797
-Bobby?
-Yeah?

50
00:07:44,965 --> 00:07:46,674
-lt's me.
-Who's me?

51
00:07:46,842 --> 00:07:47,925
Dean.

52
00:07:48,093 --> 00:07:50,177
[LINE DISCONNECTS,
DIAL TONE HUMS]

53
00:07:56,768 --> 00:07:57,977
[LINE RINGlNG]

54
00:07:58,145 --> 00:08:00,187
BOBBY: Who is this?
-Bobby, listen to me.

55
00:08:00,355 --> 00:08:02,898
This ain't funny.
Call again and l'll kill you.

56
00:08:03,066 --> 00:08:04,650
[LINE DISCONNECTS,
DIAL TONE HUMS]

57
00:08:13,118 --> 00:08:15,202
[ENGINE SPUTTERlNG]

58
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:18,956
Come on, come on, come on.

59
00:08:19,124 --> 00:08:20,624
[ENGINE STARTS]

60
00:08:29,759 --> 00:08:31,969
[POUNDING ON DOOR]

61
00:08:37,934 --> 00:08:38,976
[CHUCKLES]

62
00:08:41,354 --> 00:08:42,771
Surprise.

63
00:08:43,565 --> 00:08:45,566
I-- l don't....

64
00:08:46,443 --> 00:08:48,027
Yeah, me neither.

65
00:08:49,863 --> 00:08:51,614
But here I am.

66
00:08:54,576 --> 00:08:55,993
[GRUNTlNG]

67
00:08:56,161 --> 00:08:57,494
Bobby.

68
00:08:57,662 --> 00:08:59,955
-Bobby, it's me.
-My ass.

69
00:09:00,123 --> 00:09:02,124
Wait. Your name
is Robert Stephen Singer.

70
00:09:02,292 --> 00:09:04,668
You became a hunter
after your wife got possessed.

71
00:09:04,836 --> 00:09:07,379
You're about the closest thing
I have to a father.

72
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:10,591
Bobby, it's me.

73
00:09:13,762 --> 00:09:16,847
[CHAIR SLlDES]

74
00:09:20,143 --> 00:09:21,310
Heh.

75
00:09:21,519 --> 00:09:22,603
[GRUNTlNG]

76
00:09:22,771 --> 00:09:25,397
-l am not a Shapeshifter.
-Then you're a revenant.

77
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:31,362
All right, if I was either,
could l do this with a silver knife?

78
00:09:36,660 --> 00:09:38,202
[DEAN GRUNTS]

79
00:09:41,873 --> 00:09:43,040
Dean?

80
00:09:44,042 --> 00:09:46,210
That's what l've been
trying to tell you.

81
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:50,297
[CRIES]

82
00:09:59,933 --> 00:10:03,227
-lt's good to see you, boy.
-Yeah, you too.

83
00:10:04,813 --> 00:10:08,065
But how did you bust out?

84
00:10:08,233 --> 00:10:09,817
I don't know.

85
00:10:11,152 --> 00:10:13,112
I just....

86
00:10:13,363 --> 00:10:15,364
I just woke up in a pine b--

87
00:10:21,788 --> 00:10:24,999
-l'm not a demon either, you know.
-Sorry.

88
00:10:25,166 --> 00:10:26,792
Can't be too careful.

89
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:32,214
That don't make a lick of sense.

90
00:10:32,382 --> 00:10:34,383
Yeah.
Yeah, you're preaching to the choir.

91
00:10:35,427 --> 00:10:39,013
Dean, your chest was ribbons.
Your insides were slop.

92
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:41,181
And you've been buried four months.

93
00:10:41,349 --> 00:10:44,101
If you could slip out of hell
and back in your meat--

94
00:10:44,269 --> 00:10:46,854
I know, I should look
like a "Thriller" video reject.

95
00:10:47,022 --> 00:10:50,316
-What do you remember?
-Not much.

96
00:10:50,942 --> 00:10:53,027
I remember
I was a Hellhound's chew toy.

97
00:10:53,570 --> 00:10:56,030
And then lights out.

98
00:10:56,197 --> 00:10:59,074
Then l come to 6 feet under.
That was it.

99
00:11:01,453 --> 00:11:04,038
Sam's number's not working.
He's not...?

100
00:11:04,205 --> 00:11:06,957
Oh, he's alive, as far as I know.

101
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:09,877
Good.

102
00:11:11,546 --> 00:11:15,424
-What do you mean, as far as you know?
-l haven't talked to him for months.

103
00:11:15,592 --> 00:11:18,927
-You just let him go off by himself?
-He was dead set on it.

104
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:22,931
-You should have been looking after him.
-l tried.

105
00:11:23,099 --> 00:11:25,267
These last months haven't been easy,
you know.

106
00:11:25,435 --> 00:11:28,437
For him or me. We had to bury you.

107
00:11:28,605 --> 00:11:30,105
Why did you bury me, anyway?

108
00:11:30,273 --> 00:11:34,693
I wanted you salted and burned.
Usual drill, but Sam wouldn't have it.

109
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:38,322
-l'm glad he won that one.
-He said you'd need a body...

110
00:11:38,490 --> 00:11:40,616
...when he got you back home
somehow.

111
00:11:40,784 --> 00:11:43,243
-That's about all he said.
-What do you mean?

112
00:11:43,411 --> 00:11:47,498
He was quiet. Real quiet.

113
00:11:47,874 --> 00:11:51,168
Then he just took off.
Wouldn't return my calls.

114
00:11:51,336 --> 00:11:54,338
I tried to find him,
but he don't wanna be found.

115
00:11:54,506 --> 00:11:55,881
Damn it, Sammy.

116
00:11:56,424 --> 00:11:58,634
-What?
-Oh, he got me home okay.

117
00:11:58,802 --> 00:12:00,886
But whatever he did, it is bad mojo.

118
00:12:01,054 --> 00:12:03,597
-What makes you sure?
-You should've seen the grave.

119
00:12:03,765 --> 00:12:06,558
It was like a nuke went off.
Then there was this....

120
00:12:06,726 --> 00:12:08,977
This force, this presence,
I don't know.

121
00:12:09,145 --> 00:12:12,481
But it blew past me at a fill-up joint.

122
00:12:14,484 --> 00:12:16,151
And then this.

123
00:12:22,575 --> 00:12:26,370
-What in the hell?
-lt was like a demon just yanked me out.

124
00:12:26,538 --> 00:12:28,372
Or rode me out.

125
00:12:28,540 --> 00:12:30,791
-But why?
-To hold up their end of the bargain.

126
00:12:30,959 --> 00:12:32,501
You think Sam made a deal?

127
00:12:33,378 --> 00:12:35,462
That's what l would have done.

128
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:36,713
[WOMAN SPEAKS INDlSTlNCTLY
OVER PHONE]

129
00:12:36,881 --> 00:12:40,717
Yeah, hi, l have a cell phone account
with you guys and I lost my phone.

130
00:12:40,885 --> 00:12:43,762
I was wondering if you could
turn the GPS on for me.

131
00:12:44,097 --> 00:12:47,516
-Yeah, the name's Wedge Antilles.
-The last four digits of your social?

132
00:12:47,684 --> 00:12:50,436
-Social is 2474.
-Thank you, sir, it's active.

133
00:12:50,603 --> 00:12:52,312
Thank you.

134
00:12:55,733 --> 00:12:57,443
How'd you know he'd use that name?

135
00:12:57,610 --> 00:12:59,653
You kidding me?
What don't I know about that kid?

136
00:12:59,821 --> 00:13:00,863
[TYPlNG]

137
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:08,078
Hey, Bobby.
What's the deal with the liquor store?

138
00:13:08,246 --> 00:13:09,788
Your parents are out of town?

139
00:13:09,956 --> 00:13:11,957
Like l said...

140
00:13:12,125 --> 00:13:16,128
...last few months
ain't been all that easy.

141
00:13:18,214 --> 00:13:19,840
Right.

142
00:13:21,634 --> 00:13:22,885
[BEEPlNG]

143
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:29,016
-Sam's in Pontiac, lllinois.
-Right near where you were planted.

144
00:13:29,184 --> 00:13:32,186
Right where l popped up.
A coincidence, don't you think?

145
00:13:35,565 --> 00:13:37,649
[ROCK MUSlC PLAYlNG INSIDE]

146
00:13:45,116 --> 00:13:46,533
So where is it?

147
00:13:49,329 --> 00:13:50,370
Where's what?

148
00:13:51,039 --> 00:13:53,290
The pizza that takes two guys
to deliver?

149
00:13:53,458 --> 00:13:55,918
I think we got the wrong room.

150
00:14:05,929 --> 00:14:07,387
Hey, Sammy.

151
00:14:07,555 --> 00:14:09,640
[BREATHlNG HEAVlLY]

152
00:14:16,439 --> 00:14:18,524
[GRUNTlNG]

153
00:14:19,609 --> 00:14:21,443
-Who are you?
-Like you didn't do this?

154
00:14:21,611 --> 00:14:23,862
-Do what?
BOBBY: It's him. lt's him, Sam.

155
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:26,406
I've been through this already.
It's really him.

156
00:14:28,034 --> 00:14:29,368
What...?

157
00:14:31,579 --> 00:14:33,330
I know.

158
00:14:34,332 --> 00:14:36,041
I look fantastic, huh?

159
00:14:43,466 --> 00:14:45,717
[SNlFFLING]

160
00:14:56,437 --> 00:14:59,398
So are you two, like, together?

161
00:14:59,566 --> 00:15:02,234
What? No. No.

162
00:15:04,237 --> 00:15:05,779
He's my brother.

163
00:15:07,365 --> 00:15:08,407
O-oh--

164
00:15:08,575 --> 00:15:12,703
Got it, I guess.
Look, l should probably go.

165
00:15:12,870 --> 00:15:15,455
Yeah, yeah.
That's probably a good idea. Sorry.

166
00:15:17,792 --> 00:15:21,128
-So call me.
-Yeah, yeah. Sure thing, Kathy.

167
00:15:21,296 --> 00:15:22,546
Chrissy.

168
00:15:23,464 --> 00:15:24,840
Right.

169
00:15:39,355 --> 00:15:41,523
So tell me, what'd it cost?

170
00:15:42,025 --> 00:15:44,818
The girl? Heh. l don't pay, Dean.

171
00:15:44,986 --> 00:15:47,112
That's not funny, Sam.

172
00:15:47,739 --> 00:15:49,072
To bring me back.

173
00:15:50,033 --> 00:15:51,283
What'd it cost?

174
00:15:51,451 --> 00:15:53,619
Was it just your soul,
or something worse?

175
00:15:53,786 --> 00:15:55,954
-You think l made a deal?
-That's what we think.

176
00:15:56,122 --> 00:15:57,331
Well, l didn't.

177
00:15:59,042 --> 00:16:00,917
Don't lie to me.

178
00:16:01,419 --> 00:16:02,544
I'm not lying.

179
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:06,673
So, what, now l'm off the hook
and you're on, is that it?

180
00:16:06,841 --> 00:16:10,469
You're some demon's bitch boy?
I didn't wanna be saved like this.

181
00:16:10,637 --> 00:16:13,221
Look, Dean,
I wish I had done it, all right?

182
00:16:13,556 --> 00:16:16,350
There's no other way
this could have gone. Tell the truth.

183
00:16:16,517 --> 00:16:19,770
I tried everything. That's the truth.
Opening the Devil's Gate...

184
00:16:19,937 --> 00:16:23,940
...hell, l tried to bargain, Dean,
but no demon would deal, all right?

185
00:16:25,401 --> 00:16:29,905
You were rotting in hell for months.
For months, and l couldn't stop it.

186
00:16:31,407 --> 00:16:33,950
So l'm sorry. lt wasn't me, all right?

187
00:16:36,829 --> 00:16:38,246
Dean, I'm sorry.

188
00:16:40,124 --> 00:16:41,541
It's okay, Sammy.

189
00:16:43,878 --> 00:16:46,213
You don't have to apologize.
I believe you.

190
00:16:48,341 --> 00:16:53,387
Don't get me wrong, I am gladdened
that Sam's soul remains intact...

191
00:16:53,554 --> 00:16:55,514
...but it does raise a sticky question.

192
00:16:57,934 --> 00:17:01,019
If he didn't pull me out then what did?

193
00:17:13,408 --> 00:17:16,785
So, what were you doing here if you
weren't digging me out of my grave?

194
00:17:16,994 --> 00:17:19,955
Well, once I figured out
I couldn't save you...

195
00:17:20,415 --> 00:17:23,375
...l started hunting down Lilith,
trying to get some payback.

196
00:17:23,543 --> 00:17:25,210
BOBBY:
All by yourself?

197
00:17:25,378 --> 00:17:27,045
Who do you think you are,
your old man?

198
00:17:27,213 --> 00:17:28,797
Uh....

199
00:17:29,006 --> 00:17:33,135
Yeah, l'm sorry, Bobby. I should
have called. l was pretty messed up.

200
00:17:33,594 --> 00:17:36,263
Oh, yeah. I really feel your pain.

201
00:17:37,974 --> 00:17:39,057
[SAM CHUCKLES]

202
00:17:39,225 --> 00:17:42,477
Anyways, l was tracking these demons
out in Tennessee...

203
00:17:42,645 --> 00:17:45,313
...and out of nowhere,
they took a left, booked up here.

204
00:17:45,523 --> 00:17:46,815
-When?
-Yesterday morning.

205
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:48,442
When I busted out.

206
00:17:48,609 --> 00:17:51,278
You think these demons are here
because of you?

207
00:17:51,988 --> 00:17:53,113
But why?

208
00:17:53,281 --> 00:17:56,283
I don't know. But some badass demon
drags me out, now this?

209
00:17:56,451 --> 00:18:00,579
-lt's gotta be connected somehow.
-How you feeling, anyway?

210
00:18:00,955 --> 00:18:01,997
I'm a little hungry.

211
00:18:02,165 --> 00:18:04,624
No, I mean, do you feel like yourself?

212
00:18:04,792 --> 00:18:07,836
-Anything strange or different?
-Or demonic?

213
00:18:08,045 --> 00:18:10,422
Bobby, how many times
I have to prove l'm me?

214
00:18:10,590 --> 00:18:14,092
Listen, no demon's letting you loose
out of the goodness of their hearts.

215
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:16,136
They gotta have
something nasty planned.

216
00:18:16,304 --> 00:18:17,763
-l feel fine.
SAM: We don't know

217
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:20,182
...what they're planning.
We got a pile of questions...

218
00:18:20,349 --> 00:18:22,350
...and no shovel. We need help.

219
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:25,187
I know a psychic
a few hours from here.

220
00:18:25,354 --> 00:18:28,273
Something this big,
maybe she's heard the other side talking.

221
00:18:28,441 --> 00:18:31,568
-Hell, yeah, it's worth a shot.
-l'll be right back.

222
00:18:33,821 --> 00:18:35,530
Hey, wait.

223
00:18:36,199 --> 00:18:37,699
You probably want this back.

224
00:18:44,457 --> 00:18:45,791
Thanks.

225
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:48,210
Yeah, don't mention it.

226
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:52,297
Hey, Dean, what was it like?

227
00:18:54,050 --> 00:18:55,801
What, hell?

228
00:18:57,220 --> 00:18:59,638
I don't know.
I must have blacked it out.

229
00:19:02,225 --> 00:19:03,850
I don't remember a damn thing.

230
00:19:06,229 --> 00:19:08,897
-Thank God for that.
-Yeah.

231
00:19:14,529 --> 00:19:16,029
[SNlFFS]

232
00:19:19,408 --> 00:19:21,493
[VOICES HOWLING]

233
00:19:34,090 --> 00:19:37,384
She's about four hours
down the interstate.

234
00:19:38,553 --> 00:19:40,512
Try to keep up.

235
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:44,099
I assume you'll wanna drive.

236
00:19:44,267 --> 00:19:45,600
[LAUGHS]

237
00:19:45,768 --> 00:19:48,019
I almost forgot.

238
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:50,730
Hey, sweetheart, you miss me?

239
00:19:55,361 --> 00:19:56,570
Oh.

240
00:20:00,575 --> 00:20:02,951
-What the hell is that?
-That's an iPod jack.

241
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:04,786
You were supposed to take care of her...

242
00:20:04,954 --> 00:20:06,371
-...not douche her up.
-Heh.

243
00:20:06,747 --> 00:20:08,456
Dean, I thought it was my car.

244
00:20:11,961 --> 00:20:13,295
[ENGINE STARTS]

245
00:20:13,462 --> 00:20:17,048
[JASON MANNS' "VlSlON" PLAYS]

246
00:20:17,258 --> 00:20:18,383
Really?

247
00:20:20,970 --> 00:20:22,470
[MUSlC STOPS]

248
00:20:24,807 --> 00:20:26,933
DEAN: There's still one thing
that's bothering me.

249
00:20:27,101 --> 00:20:28,143
Yeah?

250
00:20:28,311 --> 00:20:31,438
Yeah, the night that l bit it. Or got bit.

251
00:20:32,398 --> 00:20:34,900
How'd you make it out?
Lilith was gonna kill you.

252
00:20:35,067 --> 00:20:38,278
-She tried. She couldn't.
-What do you mean, she couldn't?

253
00:20:38,446 --> 00:20:41,907
She fired this, like,
burning light at me.

254
00:20:42,074 --> 00:20:43,158
And...

255
00:20:44,327 --> 00:20:45,785
...it didn't leave a scratch.

256
00:20:45,953 --> 00:20:48,163
Like l was immune or something.

257
00:20:48,414 --> 00:20:50,165
-lmmune?
-Yeah. Heh.

258
00:20:50,333 --> 00:20:52,584
I don't know who was more surprised,
her or me.

259
00:20:52,752 --> 00:20:53,793
[SIGHS]

260
00:20:53,961 --> 00:20:55,795
She left pretty fast after that.

261
00:20:56,839 --> 00:20:58,298
Huh.

262
00:20:58,507 --> 00:21:01,843
-What about Ruby? Where's she?
-Dead, or in hell.

263
00:21:05,014 --> 00:21:08,183
You've been using
your freaky ESP stuff?

264
00:21:08,351 --> 00:21:10,185
-No.
-You sure about that?

265
00:21:10,353 --> 00:21:14,481
I mean, now that you've got immunity,
whatever the hell that is...

266
00:21:14,649 --> 00:21:16,983
...just wondering
what other weirdo crap you got.

267
00:21:17,151 --> 00:21:18,318
Nothing, Dean.

268
00:21:18,486 --> 00:21:21,529
You didn't want me to go
down that road, so l didn't go.

269
00:21:21,739 --> 00:21:23,823
It was practically your dying wish.

270
00:21:25,868 --> 00:21:27,535
Yeah, well, let's keep it that way.

271
00:21:38,839 --> 00:21:40,715
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

272
00:21:41,550 --> 00:21:42,884
[BOTH LAUGH]

273
00:21:43,052 --> 00:21:45,220
-Bobby.
-Pam.

274
00:21:45,388 --> 00:21:46,721
[BOTH GRUNT, LAUGH]

275
00:21:46,889 --> 00:21:48,390
BOBBY:
You're a sight for sore eyes.

276
00:21:49,266 --> 00:21:50,809
So are these the boys?

277
00:21:50,977 --> 00:21:54,980
Sam, Dean, Pamela Barnes.
Best damn psychic in the state.

278
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:56,398
-Hey.
-Hi.

279
00:21:56,565 --> 00:21:57,983
Mm-mm-mm.

280
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:00,235
[CHUCKLES]

281
00:22:00,403 --> 00:22:01,528
Dean Winchester.

282
00:22:01,696 --> 00:22:04,406
Out of the fire
and back in the frying pan, huh?

283
00:22:04,573 --> 00:22:05,991
Makes you a rare individual.

284
00:22:06,867 --> 00:22:08,702
If you say so.

285
00:22:08,911 --> 00:22:10,662
Come on in.

286
00:22:11,163 --> 00:22:12,205
[CHUCKLES]

287
00:22:12,373 --> 00:22:14,582
So you hear anything?

288
00:22:14,792 --> 00:22:18,586
Well, l Ouija'd my way
through a dozen spirits.

289
00:22:18,796 --> 00:22:21,381
No one seems to know
who broke your boy out or why.

290
00:22:21,549 --> 00:22:23,591
-So, what's next?
-A seance, I think.

291
00:22:23,759 --> 00:22:25,427
See if we can see who did the deed.

292
00:22:25,594 --> 00:22:27,762
You're not gonna summon
the damn thing here?

293
00:22:27,930 --> 00:22:30,432
No. I just wanna
get a sneak peek at it.

294
00:22:30,599 --> 00:22:33,184
Like a crystal ball without the crystal.

295
00:22:34,020 --> 00:22:35,103
I'm game.

296
00:22:36,772 --> 00:22:37,814
[SIGHS]

297
00:22:47,033 --> 00:22:48,074
PAMELA:
Let's see.

298
00:22:53,247 --> 00:22:54,748
Who's Jesse?

299
00:22:54,915 --> 00:22:56,041
[PAMELA LAUGHS]

300
00:22:56,208 --> 00:22:59,252
-Well, it wasn't forever.
-His loss.

301
00:23:00,129 --> 00:23:01,546
Heh.

302
00:23:02,798 --> 00:23:04,966
Might be your gain.

303
00:23:08,471 --> 00:23:10,972
-Dude, l'm so in.
-Yeah, she's gonna eat you alive.

304
00:23:11,140 --> 00:23:13,308
Hey, I just got out ofjail. Bring it.

305
00:23:13,476 --> 00:23:16,144
-Ha.
-You're invited too, grumpy.

306
00:23:16,896 --> 00:23:18,146
You are not invited.

307
00:23:20,775 --> 00:23:22,400
Right.

308
00:23:22,860 --> 00:23:25,111
Take each other's hands.

309
00:23:27,156 --> 00:23:30,825
And l need to touch something
our mystery monster touched.

310
00:23:30,993 --> 00:23:32,077
Whoa!

311
00:23:32,244 --> 00:23:34,996
-Well, he didn't touch me there.
-Ha-ha-ha. My mistake.

312
00:23:38,501 --> 00:23:39,876
[DEAN CLEARS THROAT]

313
00:23:48,636 --> 00:23:50,178
PAMELA:
Okay.

314
00:23:57,186 --> 00:23:59,521
[CHANTING]
l invoke, conjure and command you...

315
00:23:59,688 --> 00:24:01,689
...appear unto me before this circle.

316
00:24:01,899 --> 00:24:11,116
l invoke, conjure and command you,
appear unto me before this circle.

317
00:24:11,283 --> 00:24:13,952
l invoke, conjure and command you--

318
00:24:14,120 --> 00:24:15,662
Castiel?

319
00:24:15,830 --> 00:24:18,331
No. Sorry, Castiel, l don't scare easy.

320
00:24:18,499 --> 00:24:19,666
Castiel?

321
00:24:19,834 --> 00:24:22,627
Its name. lt's whispering to me,
warning me to turn back.

322
00:24:22,795 --> 00:24:30,802
l conjure and command you,
show me your face.

323
00:24:30,970 --> 00:24:33,513
-I conjure and command you--
-Maybe we should stop.

324
00:24:33,681 --> 00:24:37,058
I almost got it.
I command you, show me your face.

325
00:24:37,226 --> 00:24:38,476
Show me your face now.

326
00:24:39,478 --> 00:24:41,563
[SCREAMlNG]

327
00:24:47,236 --> 00:24:49,237
BOBBY:
Call 91 1 .

328
00:24:52,741 --> 00:24:54,576
[GASPlNG]

329
00:24:55,536 --> 00:24:56,995
[SOBBlNG]

330
00:24:57,329 --> 00:25:01,249
I can't see. l can't see.

331
00:25:01,417 --> 00:25:03,251
-Oh, God.
SAM: We have an injured woman.

332
00:25:04,879 --> 00:25:06,588
PAMELA:
Oh, God.

333
00:25:12,344 --> 00:25:14,721
-Be up in a jiff.
-Yeah, you bet.

334
00:25:14,889 --> 00:25:19,058
-What'd Bobby say?
-Uh, Pam's stable and out of ICU.

335
00:25:19,226 --> 00:25:20,810
And blind because of us.

336
00:25:20,978 --> 00:25:22,812
Still no clue what we're dealing with.

337
00:25:22,980 --> 00:25:24,439
-That's not entirely true.
-No?

338
00:25:24,607 --> 00:25:26,441
We got a name. Castiel or whatever.

339
00:25:26,609 --> 00:25:28,943
With the right mumbo jumbo,
we can summon him.

340
00:25:29,111 --> 00:25:30,570
You're crazy. Absolutely not.

341
00:25:30,738 --> 00:25:32,739
We'll work him over.
After what he did?

342
00:25:32,907 --> 00:25:35,783
Pam took a peek at him
and her eyes burned out of her skull.

343
00:25:35,951 --> 00:25:38,161
-You wanna have a face-to-face?
-Got a better idea?

344
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:41,664
Yeah, as a matter of fact l do.
I followed some demons to town, right?

345
00:25:41,874 --> 00:25:44,083
-Okay.
-So we go find them.

346
00:25:44,251 --> 00:25:47,003
Someone's gotta know something
about something.

347
00:25:47,755 --> 00:25:49,297
Thanks.

348
00:25:51,300 --> 00:25:52,800
[SIGHS]

349
00:25:54,595 --> 00:25:55,970
You angling for a tip?

350
00:25:56,138 --> 00:25:58,640
I'm sorry,
I thought you were looking for us.

351
00:26:17,159 --> 00:26:18,993
Dean.

352
00:26:19,161 --> 00:26:21,287
To hell and back.

353
00:26:21,455 --> 00:26:23,331
Aren't you a lucky duck?

354
00:26:23,499 --> 00:26:27,794
-That's me.
-So you get to just stroll out of the pit?

355
00:26:27,962 --> 00:26:30,713
Tell me, what makes you so special?

356
00:26:30,923 --> 00:26:34,008
I like to think
it's because of my perky nipples.

357
00:26:36,178 --> 00:26:38,012
I don't know.

358
00:26:38,180 --> 00:26:40,682
Wasn't my doing.
I don't know who pulled me out.

359
00:26:40,849 --> 00:26:42,684
Right. You don't.

360
00:26:42,851 --> 00:26:46,229
-No, I don't.
-Lying's a sin, you know.

361
00:26:49,358 --> 00:26:50,358
I'm not lying.

362
00:26:53,487 --> 00:26:56,698
I'd like to find out, so if you
wouldn't mind enlightening me, Flo....

363
00:26:57,199 --> 00:27:00,994
Mind your tone with me, boy.
I'll drag you back to hell myself.

364
00:27:08,210 --> 00:27:09,544
No, you won't.

365
00:27:09,712 --> 00:27:11,045
-No?
-No.

366
00:27:11,213 --> 00:27:13,047
If you were,
you'd have done it already.

367
00:27:13,215 --> 00:27:16,342
Fact is, you don't know
who cut me loose.

368
00:27:16,510 --> 00:27:20,346
You're just as spooked as we are.
And you're looking for answers.

369
00:27:22,850 --> 00:27:25,018
Well, maybe it was
some turbo-charged spirit.

370
00:27:25,227 --> 00:27:28,563
Hmm? Or Godzilla.

371
00:27:28,731 --> 00:27:30,606
Or some big, bad, boss demon.

372
00:27:30,774 --> 00:27:34,193
But l'm guessing at your pay grade,
that they don't tell you squat.

373
00:27:34,361 --> 00:27:38,614
Because whoever it was,
they want me out.

374
00:27:39,116 --> 00:27:40,908
And they're a lot stronger than you.

375
00:27:43,579 --> 00:27:45,413
So go ahead, send me back.

376
00:27:45,581 --> 00:27:48,249
Don't crawl to me
when they show up on your doorstep...

377
00:27:48,417 --> 00:27:50,043
...with Vaseline and a fire hose.

378
00:27:50,210 --> 00:27:53,755
I'm gonna reach down your throat
and rip out your lungs.

379
00:28:11,106 --> 00:28:12,106
That's what I thought.

380
00:28:14,026 --> 00:28:15,777
Let's go, Sam.

381
00:28:27,831 --> 00:28:29,916
For the pie.

382
00:28:32,127 --> 00:28:33,961
[LOW GROWL]

383
00:28:34,129 --> 00:28:36,339
[DOOR OPENS]

384
00:28:39,802 --> 00:28:43,471
-Holy crap, that was close.
-We're not gonna leave them, are we?

385
00:28:43,639 --> 00:28:46,516
There's three of them, probably more.
We only got one knife.

386
00:28:46,683 --> 00:28:48,976
I've been killing more demons
than that lately.

387
00:28:49,144 --> 00:28:51,813
Not anymore.
The smarter brother's back in town.

388
00:28:51,980 --> 00:28:53,648
Dean, we gotta take them.

389
00:28:53,816 --> 00:28:55,608
-They are dangerous.
-They're scared.

390
00:28:55,776 --> 00:28:58,027
Scared of whatever had the juice
to yank me out.

391
00:28:58,195 --> 00:29:00,822
We're dealing with a bad mofo here.
One job at a time.

392
00:29:12,334 --> 00:29:14,127
[LOCK CLICKS]

393
00:29:24,972 --> 00:29:26,639
[ENGINE STARTS]

394
00:29:49,872 --> 00:29:51,914
[STATIC HISSlNG,
VOICES OVER RADlO COME AND GO]

395
00:30:22,571 --> 00:30:24,697
[HlGH-PITCHED HUM]

396
00:30:32,164 --> 00:30:34,248
[GLASS SHATTERlNG]

397
00:30:40,756 --> 00:30:42,381
[GRUNTlNG]

398
00:30:50,766 --> 00:30:52,225
[SCREAMS]

399
00:30:52,434 --> 00:30:54,810
BOBBY:
Dean. Dean!

400
00:31:04,029 --> 00:31:05,988
How you doing, kid?

401
00:31:06,156 --> 00:31:08,616
Aside from the church bells
ringing in my head...

402
00:31:08,784 --> 00:31:10,618
...peachy.

403
00:31:10,953 --> 00:31:13,329
[DlALING]

404
00:31:13,539 --> 00:31:15,623
[CELL PHONE RlNGS]

405
00:31:18,794 --> 00:31:20,127
-Hey.
-What are you doing?

406
00:31:20,295 --> 00:31:22,964
-Couldn't sleep. Went to get a burger.
-ln my car?

407
00:31:23,131 --> 00:31:24,966
Force of habit. What you doing up?

408
00:31:25,133 --> 00:31:28,302
Well, Bobby's back.
We're going to grab a beer.

409
00:31:30,556 --> 00:31:32,974
All right, well, spill some for me, huh?

410
00:31:33,141 --> 00:31:35,476
Done. I'll catch you later.

411
00:31:44,152 --> 00:31:47,071
-Why the hell didn't you tell him?
-He'd just try to stop us.

412
00:31:47,281 --> 00:31:49,657
-From what?
-Summoning this thing.

413
00:31:50,409 --> 00:31:53,327
-lt's time we face it head on.
-You can't be serious.

414
00:31:53,495 --> 00:31:55,162
As a heart attack.

415
00:31:55,831 --> 00:31:58,374
-lt's high noon, baby.
-We don't know what it is.

416
00:31:58,542 --> 00:32:00,543
It could be a demon,
it could be anything.

417
00:32:00,711 --> 00:32:02,837
So then we gotta be ready
for anything.

418
00:32:05,340 --> 00:32:09,343
We got the bigtime magic knife,
you got an arsenal in the trunk.

419
00:32:09,511 --> 00:32:11,012
This is a bad idea.

420
00:32:11,179 --> 00:32:13,848
Couldn't agree more,
but what other choice do we have?

421
00:32:14,016 --> 00:32:15,182
We could choose life.

422
00:32:15,350 --> 00:32:17,935
Whatever this is, whatever it wants,
it's after me.

423
00:32:18,103 --> 00:32:20,730
That much we know, right?
Well, l got no place to hide.

424
00:32:20,897 --> 00:32:24,942
I can either get caught with my pants
down again, or we can make our stand.

425
00:32:25,110 --> 00:32:27,862
Dean, we could use Sam for this.

426
00:32:28,030 --> 00:32:29,530
No, he's better off where he is.

427
00:32:29,865 --> 00:32:31,949
[MUSlC PLAYlNG IN DlSTANCE]

428
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:07,151
[SIGHS]

429
00:33:12,741 --> 00:33:14,241
[SAM GRUNTS]

430
00:33:22,125 --> 00:33:23,751
[GRUNTlNG]

431
00:33:45,774 --> 00:33:46,941
Your eyes.

432
00:33:47,109 --> 00:33:49,151
I could still smell your soul
a mile away.

433
00:33:50,028 --> 00:33:52,029
It was here. You saw it.

434
00:33:52,656 --> 00:33:55,616
-l saw it.
-What was it?

435
00:33:55,784 --> 00:33:57,159
[SOBS]

436
00:33:57,703 --> 00:34:00,663
It's the end.
We're dead. We're all dead.

437
00:34:01,623 --> 00:34:02,790
What did you see?

438
00:34:04,334 --> 00:34:05,459
Go to hell.

439
00:34:08,797 --> 00:34:12,550
Funny, l was gonna say
the same thing to you.

440
00:34:13,635 --> 00:34:15,678
[GASPlNG]

441
00:34:15,929 --> 00:34:17,972
[GAGGlNG]

442
00:34:48,879 --> 00:34:50,504
[EXHALES]

443
00:35:02,893 --> 00:35:03,934
[SIGHS]

444
00:35:04,102 --> 00:35:05,227
Damn it.

445
00:35:05,395 --> 00:35:06,729
[DOOR OPENS]

446
00:35:09,191 --> 00:35:12,735
Getting pretty slick there, Sam.
Better all the time.

447
00:35:20,118 --> 00:35:22,745
What the hell's going on
around here, Ruby?

448
00:35:23,997 --> 00:35:25,122
I wish I knew.

449
00:35:26,500 --> 00:35:29,084
We were thinking
some high-level demon pulled Dean out.

450
00:35:29,252 --> 00:35:30,377
No way.

451
00:35:30,545 --> 00:35:32,880
Sam, human souls
don't just walk out of hell...

452
00:35:33,048 --> 00:35:34,715
...and back into their bodies easy.

453
00:35:34,883 --> 00:35:38,761
The sky bleeds, the ground quakes.
It's cosmic.

454
00:35:40,514 --> 00:35:42,640
No demon can swing that.

455
00:35:43,225 --> 00:35:45,392
Not Lilith.

456
00:35:46,019 --> 00:35:48,562
-Not anybody.
-Then what can?

457
00:35:49,314 --> 00:35:51,065
Nothing l've ever seen before.

458
00:36:05,121 --> 00:36:07,498
It's a hell of an art project
you got going there.

459
00:36:07,666 --> 00:36:11,085
Traps and talismans
from every faith on the globe.

460
00:36:11,419 --> 00:36:12,670
How you doing?

461
00:36:12,838 --> 00:36:15,256
Stakes, iron, silver, salt, the knife.

462
00:36:15,423 --> 00:36:17,633
We're set to catch
anything I've ever heard of.

463
00:36:18,426 --> 00:36:20,135
This is still a bad idea.

464
00:36:20,303 --> 00:36:22,555
Yeah, Bobby,
I heard you the first ten times.

465
00:36:23,598 --> 00:36:25,432
What do you say
we ring the dinner bell?

466
00:36:40,156 --> 00:36:42,950
[SPEAKS IN LATIN]

467
00:36:43,451 --> 00:36:45,828
So, million-dollar question:

468
00:36:45,996 --> 00:36:48,622
You gonna tell Dean
about what we're doing?

469
00:36:49,624 --> 00:36:52,459
Yeah, l just gotta figure out
the right way to say it.

470
00:36:54,087 --> 00:36:57,131
-Look, I just need time, okay? That's all.
-He's gonna find out.

471
00:36:57,299 --> 00:37:00,634
-lf not from you, he's gonna be pissed.
-He's gonna be pissed anyway.

472
00:37:00,802 --> 00:37:04,722
He's so hard-headed about this psychic
stuff, he'll just try and stop me.

473
00:37:04,890 --> 00:37:07,308
Maybe I'll just take a step back
for a while.

474
00:37:08,143 --> 00:37:11,312
I'm not exactly
in your brother's fan club.

475
00:37:11,479 --> 00:37:13,063
But he is your brother.

476
00:37:13,231 --> 00:37:15,649
And l'm not gonna
come between you.

477
00:37:15,817 --> 00:37:19,653
I don't know if what l'm doing is right.
Hell, I don't even know if I trust you.

478
00:37:19,821 --> 00:37:21,488
-Thanks.
-What I do know is...

479
00:37:21,656 --> 00:37:23,365
...l'm saving people...

480
00:37:23,533 --> 00:37:25,826
...and stopping demons.

481
00:37:26,745 --> 00:37:28,495
And that feels good.

482
00:37:30,123 --> 00:37:31,624
I wanna keep going.

483
00:37:33,835 --> 00:37:35,878
[BOBBY WHlSTLlNG]

484
00:37:47,766 --> 00:37:50,225
You sure you did the ritual right?

485
00:37:51,353 --> 00:37:54,730
Sorry. Touchy, touchy.

486
00:37:56,524 --> 00:37:59,360
[WlND WHlSTLlNG, LOUD THUDDlNG]

487
00:38:12,415 --> 00:38:15,376
Wishful thinking,
but maybe it's just the wind.

488
00:38:50,245 --> 00:38:51,745
Who are you?

489
00:38:51,913 --> 00:38:54,957
I'm the one who gripped you tight
and raised you from perdition.

490
00:38:55,125 --> 00:38:57,751
Yeah, thanks for that.

491
00:39:10,432 --> 00:39:11,515
[KNlFE CLATTERS]

492
00:39:12,600 --> 00:39:14,226
[YELLS]

493
00:39:25,739 --> 00:39:27,114
We need to talk, Dean.

494
00:39:29,451 --> 00:39:30,659
Alone.

495
00:39:44,007 --> 00:39:46,633
-Your friend's alive.
-Who are you?

496
00:39:46,801 --> 00:39:47,968
Castiel.

497
00:39:48,136 --> 00:39:51,055
Yeah, l figured that much.
I mean, what are you?

498
00:39:52,891 --> 00:39:54,641
I'm an angel of the Lord.

499
00:40:01,733 --> 00:40:04,068
Get the hell out of here.

500
00:40:04,319 --> 00:40:06,612
There's no such thing.

501
00:40:09,741 --> 00:40:12,159
This is your problem, Dean.

502
00:40:12,452 --> 00:40:14,745
You have no faith.

503
00:40:15,830 --> 00:40:17,956
[THUNDER CRASHlNG]

504
00:40:29,469 --> 00:40:31,512
Some angel you are.

505
00:40:31,679 --> 00:40:34,348
You burned out
that poor woman's eyes.

506
00:40:35,683 --> 00:40:38,644
I warned her
not to spy on my true form.

507
00:40:38,812 --> 00:40:41,522
It can be overwhelming to humans.

508
00:40:41,689 --> 00:40:44,691
And so can my real voice,
but you already knew that.

509
00:40:44,859 --> 00:40:47,277
You mean the gas station
and the motel?

510
00:40:48,446 --> 00:40:49,696
That was you talking?

511
00:40:51,199 --> 00:40:53,700
Buddy, next time, lower the volume.

512
00:40:53,868 --> 00:40:55,869
That was my mistake.

513
00:40:56,079 --> 00:40:59,665
Certain people, special people,
can perceive my true visage.

514
00:40:59,833 --> 00:41:02,793
I thought you would be one of them.
I was wrong.

515
00:41:03,628 --> 00:41:07,172
And what visage are you in now, huh?
What, holy tax accountant?

516
00:41:07,715 --> 00:41:11,051
This? This is a vessel.

517
00:41:11,219 --> 00:41:13,220
You're possessing some poor bastard?

518
00:41:13,388 --> 00:41:16,223
He's a devout man.
He actually prayed for this.

519
00:41:16,391 --> 00:41:19,893
Look, pal, l'm not buying what
you're selling. So who are you, really?

520
00:41:21,396 --> 00:41:22,604
I told you.

521
00:41:23,481 --> 00:41:25,065
Right.

522
00:41:25,608 --> 00:41:28,902
And why would an angel
rescue me from hell?

523
00:41:30,738 --> 00:41:32,739
Good things do happen, Dean.

524
00:41:35,994 --> 00:41:37,327
Not in my experience.

525
00:41:38,663 --> 00:41:40,622
What's the matter?

526
00:41:43,042 --> 00:41:45,919
You don't think
you deserve to be saved?

527
00:41:49,090 --> 00:41:50,507
Why'd you do it?

528
00:41:53,636 --> 00:41:55,929
Because God commanded it.

529
00:41:59,267 --> 00:42:01,351
Because we have work for you.

530
00:42:37,931 --> 00:42:39,932
[ENGLISH SDH]

